#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# conic_optimization

#% text
# `conic_optimization(f, cons, vars)` gives the point that minimizes `f` under constraints that are linear, quadratic bounds or cone memberships.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A bound `norm([x, y]) <= t` is the second-order cone constraint `x^2 + y^2 <= t^2`, `t >= 0`.

#% item
# `vector_greater_equal([v, 0], ["NormCone", n])` asks the vector `v` (its last entry the cone's axis) to lie in the second-order cone, and `["SemidefiniteCone", n]` asks a symmetric matrix to be positive semidefinite.

#% item
# A fourth argument selects "PrimalMinimumValue", "PrimalMinimizer" or "PrimalMinimizerRules" as for `quadratic_optimization`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
conic_optimization(x + 2*y, [x^2 + 2*y^2 <= 3, x + y == 2, x >= 1], [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> 5/3, y -> 1/3]

#% cell
conic_optimization(-(x + y), [x >= 0, y >= 0, x + 2*y <= 2, x^2 + y^2 <= 1], [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> 4/5, y -> 3/5]

#% cell
conic_optimization(x + y, norm([x, y]) <= 1, [x, y], "PrimalMinimumValue")
#% output
#= -2^(1/2)

